. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 *
. 
.         * Verbal description of the model:
.                 *Dependent variable: plj0620_modified: democracy: women have 
> the same rights as men
.                 *Independent variable: has_daughter (created above)
.                 
.                 *In this analysis, we assume that "plj0620" is a reasonable a
> nd straightforward proxy of support for gender equality. We hypothesize that
.                 *having a daughter correlates with support for gender equalit
> y. In line with this hypothesis, we run a linear regression of the "plj0620_m
> odified" dependent variable
.                 *on the "has_daughter" independent variable. We use robust st
> andard errors due to the increase in the variance of the dependent variable f
> or those with daughters. 
.                 *While we perform a causal hypothesis test and the main treat
> ment variable "has_daughters" should not be correlated with the remaining det
> erminants of the dependent variable
.                 *in the population, due to potential relationships arising be
> tween the treatment variable and other determinants as a result of (i) the sm
> all size of the sample, and (ii) the sample
.                 *selection procedure, we also control for the variables we be
> lieve to be among the primary determinants of the dependent variable.
. 
.         regress plj0620_modified has_daughter `control_variables', robust
note: 2.migrant omitted because of collinearity.

